cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use xpsloss in your research, please cite this software."
title: xpsloss
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
authors:
  - family-names: Sato
    given-names: Keisuke
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/skeisuke1977/xpsloss"
abstract: >-
  xpsloss implements oscillator energy-loss functions, causal dielectric response,
  and bulk inelastic scattering in Python. For normal emission from a positive
  depth in a gapless material, it calculates the effective XPS cross section
  including surface, vacuum, core-hole, and interference terms.
keywords:
  - X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy
  - dielectric response
  - electron energy loss
